  "implementation": [
    "Separate checked caller-signature refinement from definition reuse. Strictly admitted literal closures can use module-owned typed definitions inside shared child generators and through unchecked curried applications; definition emission suppresses only its own reuse.",
    "Capture and argument words are explicit parameters. Plain aggregates use the existing caller-owned result slot and load before release/rewind. Pending array destinations retain the conservative guard.",
    "Keys retain exact static closure/context, formal capture/signature/result types and semantic/physical value evidence. Qualified/goaled/abstract callbacks keep the exact old checked scalar leaf fallback.",
    "Read-only admission uses existing plannedCallback with writer planning disabled; cache keys and result shape are reconstructed after its temporary context. Per-call readerReads replays captures and explicit argument on misses and hits, including enclosing writer/loop summaries.",
    "Plain inline input keys omit only variant_index/variant_possible already recursively erased by inlineParameter. Tags, payload schemas, nominal/field names, strict semantic types and all descriptor-reader/writer refinements remain."
  ],
  "review": "Astra xhigh reviewed actual production diff, found and corrected fallback broadening and missing result evidence; final review has no blockers. Kept inactive destination-guard removal out of scope after inspecting admission.",
  "method": "Three sequential alternating fresh pairs per cell, cacheDirectory:false, profileBackend:true, optimized tier and one worker, five-second per-build cap. Source/output hashes match per pair.72completedcells plus6Gdevlanguagecontrols.",
